Lead pre-check: what the strict V8 rule does to the committed tests
Reviewer: claude (lead)
Date: 2026-10-30
Subject: B5-V8 (owner-confirmed strict rule, decisions.md 2026-10-30), before
freebuff builds it. The goal is to find out which committed "true" claims the
rule will reject, so the work order can say so in advance.

This is a probe, not an implementation. It ran in a scratch clone of b20b92d
and was reverted there. Nothing in this repo's mathd/ was changed.

====================================================================
1. The probe
====================================================================

Patch to mathd/src/verifier.rs, verify_equivalence only (the path used by
verify_identity, verify_integral and verify_factorisation). A point where
exactly one side is finite returns a marked Unverifiable instead of being
skipped. Both sides undefined still skips.

  (Ok(g), Ok(e)) arm, before the old non-finite skip:
      if g.is_finite() != e.is_finite() {
          return Verdict::Unverifiable { reason: format!("V8PROBE one-sided(nonfinite) ...") };
      }
  new arm before the old (Err(_), _) | (_, Err(_)) skip:
      (Ok(v), Err(_)) | (Err(_), Ok(v)) if v.is_finite() => {
          return Verdict::Unverifiable { reason: format!("V8PROBE one-sided(err) at {:?}", pt) };
      }

tests/corpus.rs and tests/verifier.rs were patched in the clone to print
V8PROBE verdicts instead of panicking, so one run lists every affected case.

verify_equation_solution was not patched. With no parameters it already
returns Failed on any evaluation error at a root (verifier.rs:398-429; note
that path already reports `got: f64::NAN` at line 427). The corpus has no
parameterised equations.

Runner: mathd/corpus/wasi-runner.mjs (committed in 9750779), wasm32-wasip1.

